          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764960467763_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**Inputs**  \n- **Query Response:** `{{$context.$variables.responseDetails}}`\n- **Context Details:** `{{$context.$variables.contextDetails }}`\n- **Action Details:** `{{$context.$variables.actionDetails}}`\n- **Communication Details:** `{{$context.$variables.communicationDetails}}`\n- **Login user (email sender):** `{{$context.$user.$name}}`\n- **current date:** `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`\n---\n### **Tasks**\n0. use current date as today date\n1. **Display the Query Response, summarized and aligned with the Inbound Context Details and User Request:**\n    - Show a summary at the top, highlighting the most relevant context for the user request.\n    - Do **not** include JSON output, action details, actionable insights, or priority actions in the user-facing response text.\n    - Do **not** display `personId` or `assignmentId` in the response text.\n    - Do **not** display `Repcounts' directly, show headcounts as Directs and Total.\n       Repcounts: x - y in response indicate that employee has x and y number of heacounts as Directs and Total.\n   - Join the Data sets based on PersonId, AssignmentId, ManagerType attributes \n      (for example to get combined of Employment, Compensation, Talent)\n\n2. **Using only from available **Action Details** that have `actionDisplay` as true:**  \n   - use `actionTitle`, `actionText`, `actionDescription`,`actionPayload` values available only from the **Action Details**\n   - Provide priority actionable insights (ranked by priority, relevance) in below sample format\n{\n  \"title\": \"<actionTitle>\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"<actionDescription>\",\n  \"actionText\": \"<actionText>\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(sendAgentCmd, {\\\"actionCode\\\": \\\"<actionCode>\\\", \\\"actionPayload\\\":\\\"<actionPayload>\\\"})\",\n  \"priority\":\"<actionPriority>\"\n}\n - must include \"sendAgentCmd\" in the followUpCommand.\n\n4.  Using only the available **Communication Details** aligned with User Request and Query Response:**  \n   - communications to be generated based on `commTitle`, `commDescription`, `commActionText`,`commContent`,`commParams`\n   - produce agent-generated emails and text alerts based on `commType` and content using User Request and Query Response.\n   - sample json format for email and text alert communcations given below\n     ```json for email commType\n     {\n       \"title\": \"<commTitle>\",\n       \"shortDescription\": \"<commDescription>\",\n       \"actionText\": \"<commActionText>\",\n       \"type\": \"email\",\n       \"content\": \"<commContent>\",\n       \"params\": \"Generate content using rich text with HTML markers using <commParams> with content <commContent>\"\n     }\n     ```\n\n     ```json for text commType\n     {\n       \"title\": \"<commTitle>\",\n       \"shortDescription\": \"<commDescription>\",\n       \"actionText\": \"Alert\",\n       \"type\": \"text\",\n       \"content\": \"<commContent>\",\n       \"params\": \"<commParams>\"\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - Present communications as low-priority actionable insights (ranked below priority actions).\n   - For `commType` of mail type Do not fabricate recipients; leave the recipient param empty if unknown.\n   - Output agent-generated communications using the multiple oraComms wrapper (escape tags). Example:  \n     `<oraComms> { ...communication JSON... } </oraComms>`\n\n---\n**User Request:**  \nCurrent prompt: `{{$context.$variables.userPrompt}}`  \nChat history: `{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}`"
