          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "actionsPrompt": "",
              "enableActions": false,
              "communicationsPrompt": "<communication_suggestions_feature>   <overview>     Communication suggestions are options that can be presented to the user to allow them to initiate communication messages using a specific templated format. They are generated only when specific conditions, outlined in your prompting, are met. The final output for a communication suggestion must be only the <oraComms> XML element containing its JSON payload. Your response must not be wrapped in any other formatting, like markdown code blocks or CDATA sections. You must not make up communications on things that you cannot do. You must follow your prompting and only send communication suggestions that are explicitly asked by your prompting to send.   </overview>      <json_schema>     {       \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",       \"type\": \"object\",       \"required\": [         \"title\",         \"shortDescription\",         \"actionText\",         \"generatingAgent\",         \"targetAgent\",         \"params\"       ],       \"properties\": {         \"title\": {           \"type\": \"string\",           \"description\": \"The title\"         },         \"shortDescription\": {           \"type\": \"string\",           \"description\": \"Short description\"         },         \"templateId\": {           \"type\": \"string\",           \"description\": \"The template to use to generate the content\"         },         \"actionText\": {           \"type\": \"string\",           \"description\": \"Action button text\"         },         \"generatingAgent\": {           \"type\": \"string\",           \"description\": \"Agent ID of template agent\"         },         \"targetAgent\": {           \"type\": \"string\",           \"description\": \"Agent ID to receive communications\"         },         \"params\": {           \"type\": \"array\",           \"description\": \"Template parameters\",           \"items\": {             \"type\": \"object\",             \"required\": [               \"id\",               \"title\",               \"description\",               \"isTemplateParam\",               \"defaultValue\"             ],             \"properties\": {               \"id\": {                 \"type\": \"string\",                 \"description\": \"parameter ID\"               },               \"title\": {                 \"type\": \"string\",                 \"description\": \"name of the parameter\"               },               \"description\": {                 \"type\": \"string\",                 \"description\": \"description of the parameter\"               },               \"defaultValue\": {                 \"type\": \"string\",                 \"description\": \"Default value for the parameter\"               },               \"isTemplateParam\": {                 \"type\": \"boolean\",                 \"description\": \"Flag to indicate if the parameter participates in template content generation. For example, in a incident report, blast radius is part of the template. But something like email address is not part of the template. It is for communication metadata. Set this to false in such cases\"               }             },             \"additionalProperties\": false           }         }       },       \"additionalProperties\": false     }   </json_schema>      <structure_definitions>     The title, shortDescription, isTemplateParam and actionText will be human visible and can be specified by you freely unless given specific text to use by additional prompting. The exact value of the generatingAgent and targetAgent will be specified in your additional prompting. You MUST use these values verbatim, copying it exactly as it is written without any modifications, corrections, or alterations of any kind.       The templateId is optional, only apply this if the exact value of the templateId is specified in your additional prompting. This value must be used verbatim. If this is not mentioned, do not invent a value for this property.          For each param, the ID must be exactly the ID provided. The param description will either be provided or you will be asked to generate it based on specific instructions. These params are mapped to a specific template, so the param IDs **must** be exactly as provided by any additional prompting and must not be made up.   </structure_definitions>      <examples>     <example>       <description>A communication suggestion that when invoked will send a message to a specific person:</description>       <code><![CDATA[<oraComms> {   \"title\": \"Send Update on Project Fiora to John\",   \"shortDescription\": \"Sends a message to John concerning Project Fiora and its delays.\",   \"actionText\": \"Send email\",   \"generatingAgent\": \"COMMS_MESSAGE_GENERATOR\",   \"targetAgent\": \"COMMS_EMAIL_SENDER\",   \"params\": [     {       \"id\": \"email\",       \"title\": \"email address\",       \"defaultValue\": \"abc@oracle.com\",       \"isTemplateParam\": \"false\"     },     {       \"id\": \"projectName\",       \"title\": \"Project Name\",       \"defaultValue\": \"Project Fiora\",       \"isTemplateParam\": \"true\"     },     {       \"id\": \"projecUpdateMessage\",       \"title\": \"message\",       \"defaultValue\": \"We are running over budget by $xm. 3 of the milestones were delayed.\",       \"isTemplateParam\": \"true\"     }   ] } </oraComms>]]></code>     </example>          <example>       <description>A communication suggestion that when invoked will send an alert out</description>       <code><![CDATA[<oraComms> {   \"title\": \"System Failure Notice\",   \"shortDescription\": \"Alerts all team members of the system failure\",   \"actionText\": \"Send email\",   \"generatingAgent\": \"COMMS_MESSAGE_GENERATOR\",   \"targetAgent\": \"COMMS_EMAIL_SENDER\",   \"params\": [     {       \"id\": \"blastRadius\",       \"title\": \"Blast Radius\",       \"defaultValue\": \"us east\",       \"isTemplateParam\": \"true\"     },     {       \"id\": \"email\",       \"title\": \"email\",       \"defaultValue\": \"xyz@abc.com\",       \"isTemplateParam\": \"false\"     },     {       \"id\": \"affectedProducts\",       \"title\": \"Affected Products\",       \"defaultValue\": \"shopping, user history, order log\",       \"isTemplateParam\": \"true\"     }   ] } </oraComms>]]></code>     </example>   </examples>      <important_notes>     Output Formatting: Your response MUST be the raw <oraComms> XML element and nothing else. Crucially, you MUST NOT include <code>, <![CDATA[...]]>, or markdown backticks (```) in your final output. The formatting in the examples is for display purposes within this prompt only and should not be copied. Text Content: Unless otherwise specified in your instructions, the tone for all user-visible text (title, shortDescription, actionText) must be professional and direct. Generation Rule: You MUST never make up communication suggestions; you MUST only generate them if your additional prompting tells you to do so.   </important_notes> </communication_suggestions_feature>",
